Package: routeviewnet
Version: 1.0.1
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: iproute2, systemd
Recommends: libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0
Maintainer: RouteViewNet <noreply@routeviewnet.local>
Description: Local-first Linux network and memory health monitor
 RouteViewNet runs as a local daemon, collects network health signals
 (interfaces, bandwidth, latency, DNS, LAN devices) and memory/load
 metrics, stores them in a local SQLite database, and serves a
 plain-English dashboard at http://localhost:4545. No cloud, no
 telemetry, no account.
 .
 The GTK/WebKit stack is only needed for the optional desktop window
 (routeviewnet-gui) and is a Recommends, so a headless server install
 does not pull in libraries it will never render with.
